 "scenes": [
  {
   "id": "open",
   "chapter": "",
   "type": "open",
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Go to sleep with issues. Wake up with pull requests."
    },
    {
     "text": "This is Shep: the night shift for your backlog."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "problem",
   "chapter": "The idea",
   "type": "problem",
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Coding agents are great. But today, you sit and watch them work."
    },
    {
     "text": "You babysit terminals, answer prompts, and re-run failing builds."
    },
    {
     "text": "Shep is built for the other moment: coming back to finished work."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "states",
   "chapter": "The idea",
   "type": "states",
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "The idea is simple. In the evening, you hand Shep tasks."
    },
    {
     "text": "Each task moves through five states."
    },
    {
     "text": "Queued. Working. Then Ready, or Needs you. And finally, Merged."
    },
    {
     "text": "That's the whole product."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "handover",
   "chapter": "Evening \u00b7 hand it over",
   "type": "handover",
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Handing work over looks exactly like what you already do."
    },
    {
     "text": "In Linear or Jira, add the shep label, or move the ticket to Tonight."
    },
    {
     "text": "In Slack, react with a sheep on any message."
    },
    {
     "text": "On GitHub, label the issue. Or just type it: shep add, and a sentence."
    },
    {
     "text": "You can even tell your coding agent: give this to Shep for tonight."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ack",
   "chapter": "Evening \u00b7 hand it over",
   "type": "shots",
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Shep answers right where you asked.",
     "shot": {
      "img": "SignalThread",
      "from": [
       20,
       140,
       720,
       330
      ],
      "to": [
       30,
       160,
       640,
       290
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "text": "Got it. I'll work on this tonight at eleven. No new inbox to check."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "night",
   "chapter": "Night \u00b7 the shift",
   "type": "night",
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "At eleven, the shift starts."
    },
    {
     "text": "Your own coding agent, like Claude Code or Codex, works each task in its own copy of the code, so your work in progress is never touched."
    },
    {
     "text": "The sky is the progress bar. It starts at midnight blue, and warms toward dawn as each task finishes."
    },
    {
     "text": "Every finished task is a sheep walking into the pen."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "trouble",
   "chapter": "Night \u00b7 the shift",
   "type": "trouble",
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "If a build fails, Shep reads the log and fixes it."
    },
    {
     "text": "If a task is unclear, it asks one question, and moves on to the next."
    },
    {
     "text": "And it never wakes you up."
    }
   ]
  },
